#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:1
msgid "hosted-git-info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:3
msgid ""
"This will let you identify and transform various git hosts URLs between "
"protocols.  It also can tell you what the URL is for the raw path for "
"particular file for direct access without git."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:7
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:22
msgid ""
"If the URL can't be matched with a git host, `null` will be returned.  We"
" can match git, ssh and https urls.  Additionally, we can match ssh "
"connect strings (`git@github.com:npm/hosted-git-info`) and shortcuts (eg,"
" `github:npm/hosted-git-info`).  Github specifically, is detected in the "
"case of a third, unprefixed, form: `npm/hosted-git-info`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:28
msgid "If it does match, the returned object has properties of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:30
msgid "info.type -- The short name of the service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:31
msgid "info.domain -- The domain for git protocol use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:32
msgid "info.user -- The name of the user/org on the git host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:33
msgid "info.project -- The name of the project on the git host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:35
msgid "Version Contract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:37
msgid "The major version will be bumped any time…"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:39
msgid "The constructor stops accepting URLs that it previously accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:40
msgid "A method is removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:41
msgid ""
"A method can no longer accept the number and type of arguments it "
"previously accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:42
msgid "A method can return a different type than it currently returns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:44
msgid "Implications:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:46
msgid ""
"I do not consider the specific format of the urls returned from, say "
"`.https()` to be a part of the contract.  The contract is that it will "
"return a string that can be used to fetch the repo via HTTPS.  But what "
"that string looks like, specifically, can change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:50
msgid ""
"Dropping support for a hosted git provider would constitute a breaking "
"change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:53
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:55
msgid "var info = hostedGitInfo.fromUrl(gitSpecifier[, options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:57
msgid ""
"*gitSpecifer* is a URL of a git repository or a SCP-style specifier of "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:58
msgid "*options* is an optional object. It can have the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:59
msgid ""
"*noCommittish* — If true then committishes won't be included in generated"
" URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:60
msgid "*noGitPlus* — If true then `git+` won't be prefixed on URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:62
msgid "Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:64
msgid ""
"All of the methods take the same options as the `fromUrl` factory.  "
"Options provided to a method override those provided to the constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:67
msgid "info.file(path, opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:69
msgid ""
"Given the path of a file relative to the repository, returns a URL for "
"directly fetching it from the githost.  If no committish was set then "
"`master` will be used as the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:73
msgid ""
"For example `hostedGitInfo.fromUrl(\"git@github.com:npm/hosted-git-"
"info.git#v1.0.0\").file(\"package.json\")` would return "
"`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/npm/hosted-git-"
"info/v1.0.0/package.json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:76
msgid "info.shortcut(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:78
msgid "eg, `github:npm/hosted-git-info`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:80
msgid "info.browse(path, fragment, opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:82
msgid ""
"eg, `https://github.com/npm/hosted-git-info/tree/v1.2.0`, "
"`https://github.com/npm/hosted-git-info/tree/v1.2.0/package.json`, "
"`https://github.com/npm/hosted-git-info/tree/v1.2.0/REAMDE.md#supported-"
"hosts`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:86
msgid "info.bugs(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:88
msgid "eg, `https://github.com/npm/hosted-git-info/issues`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:90
msgid "info.docs(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:92
msgid "eg, `https://github.com/npm/hosted-git-info/tree/v1.2.0#readme`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:94
msgid "info.https(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:96
msgid "eg, `git+https://github.com/npm/hosted-git-info.git`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:98
msgid "info.sshurl(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:100
msgid "eg, `git+ssh://git@github.com/npm/hosted-git-info.git`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:102
msgid "info.ssh(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:104
msgid "eg, `git@github.com:npm/hosted-git-info.git`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:106
msgid "info.path(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:108
msgid "eg, `npm/hosted-git-info`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:110
msgid "info.tarball(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:112
msgid "eg, `https://github.com/npm/hosted-git-info/archive/v1.2.0.tar.gz`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:114
msgid "info.getDefaultRepresentation()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:116
msgid ""
"Returns the default output type. The default output type is based on the "
"string you passed in to be parsed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:119
msgid "info.toString(opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:121
msgid ""
"Uses the getDefaultRepresentation to call one of the other methods to get"
" a URL for this resource. As such `hostedGitInfo.fromUrl(url).toString()`"
" will give you a normalized version of the URL that still uses the same "
"protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:125
msgid ""
"Shortcuts will still be returned as shortcuts, but the special case "
"github form of `org/project` will be normalized to `github:org/project`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:128
msgid "SSH connect strings will be normalized into `git+ssh` URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:130
msgid "Supported hosts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hosted-git-info_README.md:132
msgid ""
"Currently this supports Github, Bitbucket and Gitlab. Pull requests for "
"additional hosts welcome."
msgstr ""

